Athena with libc++ and on macOS (Apple silicon), and with libunwind's unwind.h:
- CxxUtils: feenableexcept()/fedisableexcept() for arm64 macOS (the FPCR trap enable bits;
  the existing implementation is for Intel Macs); xmalloc.cxx needs no <malloc.h>, which
  macOS does not have;
- EventContainers: <bit> included before the classes that include deleter.h inside their
  bodies (libstdc++ had always pulled it in earlier);
- AthCommonDataStore.h: std::invoke_result_t, as std::result_of_t is gone from C++20 (libc++
  removes it; libstdc++ still has it);
- ArenaBlockAlignDetail.h: <type_traits> for std::alignment_of;
- AthenaInterprocess: prctl(PR_SET_PDEATHSIG) on Linux only; AthenaMPTools: glibc's
  TEMP_FAILURE_RETRY where it is missing;
- AtlasCLHEP_RandomGenerators: the beta function from lgamma with libc++, which has no
  special mathematical functions;
- xAODRootAccess: getservbyport where there is no getservbyport_r (macOS);
- PerfMonComps: mallinfo2 only on Linux (it already returned 0 elsewhere);
- IOVDbTestAlg: msgrcv takes the message buffer as a void pointer (no struct msgbuf on macOS);
- IOVDbTPCnv: an element of std::vector<bool> passed to CORAL as a bool (libc++'s reference
  proxy overloads operator&);
- AthenaPoolUtilities: libc++'s helper templates excluded from the dictionary, which the
  iterator patterns of selection.xml match as well;
- athena_preload.sh preloads nothing on macOS, which has no LD_PRELOAD;
- CxxUtils' UnwindBacktrace: uintptr_t rather than GCC's _Unwind_Ptr and _Unwind_Word, which
  the unwind.h of libunwind does not define (on linux-64, gperftools brings it into the
  environment, ahead of GCC's);
- PathResolver: a directory it creates counts as created when it exists afterwards (libc++'s
  create_directories returns false for a path ending with a separator).

--- a/Control/CxxUtils/Root/excepts.cxx
+++ b/Control/CxxUtils/Root/excepts.cxx
@@ -23,11 +23,20 @@
                 old_excepts;  // previous masks
 
    if ( fegetenv (&fenv) ) return -1;
+#if defined(__aarch64__)
+   // Apple silicon: the trap enable bits of FPCR (the exception flags shifted by 8). The
+   // hardware may not implement trapping, as on most aarch64 machines.
+   old_excepts = (fenv.__fpcr >> 8) & FE_ALL_EXCEPT;
+
+   // unmask
+   fenv.__fpcr |= new_excepts << 8;
+#else
    old_excepts = fenv.__control & FE_ALL_EXCEPT;
 
    // unmask
    fenv.__control &= ~new_excepts;
    fenv.__mxcsr   &= ~(new_excepts << 7);
+#endif
 
    return ( fesetenv (&fenv) ? -1 : old_excepts );
 }
@@ -40,11 +49,18 @@
                 old_excepts;  // all previous masks
 
    if ( fegetenv (&fenv) ) return -1;
+#if defined(__aarch64__)
+   old_excepts = (fenv.__fpcr >> 8) & FE_ALL_EXCEPT;
+
+   // mask
+   fenv.__fpcr &= ~(static_cast<unsigned long long>(new_excepts) << 8);
+#else
    old_excepts = fenv.__control & FE_ALL_EXCEPT;
 
    // mask
    fenv.__control |= new_excepts;
    fenv.__mxcsr   |= new_excepts << 7;
+#endif
 
    return ( fesetenv (&fenv) ? -1 : old_excepts );
 }
